From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Kuraev <naoru.desu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:28:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: request a peripheral flush for RGB VSC and HDR
 SDPs

msm_dp_needs_periph_flush() asks the DPU for a peripheral flush only for
YUV 4:2:0 modes, which used to be the only streams with a VSC SDP. The
VSC SDP now also carries the colorimetry of RGB streams, and the HDR
static metadata goes out as an infoframe SDP in generic slot 2. On
controllers that put SDPs on the link with the peripheral flush, neither
packet would be latched.

Also request the flush when the connector state asks for a colorimetry
other than the default or carries HDR metadata. The DPU asks from the
encoder enable of the commit, after the state swap, so the connector
state is the one the bridge programs the packets from.

On SM8250, whose controller is revision 1.2.0.3, the packets are latched
through SDP_CFG3 instead ("drm/msm/dp: latch SDPs through SDP_CFG3 on
revision 1.2 controllers"). That was measured while the flush was still
requested only for YUV 4:2:0 modes; whether this controller also latches
them with the flush alone has not been measured.

Signed-off-by: Roman Kuraev <naoru.desu@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
index f3a1372..a86adb9 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -1306,7 +1306,20 @@ bool msm_dp_is_yuv_420_enabled(const struct msm_dp *msm_dp_display,
 bool msm_dp_needs_periph_flush(const struct msm_dp *msm_dp_display,
 			       const struct drm_display_mode *mode)
 {
-	return msm_dp_is_yuv_420_enabled(msm_dp_display, mode);
+	const struct drm_connector_state *conn_state =
+		msm_dp_display->connector->state;
+
+	if (msm_dp_is_yuv_420_enabled(msm_dp_display, mode))
+		return true;
+
+	/*
+	 * The only caller is the DPU's video encoder enable, after the state
+	 * swap of the commit, so connector->state is the new state that the
+	 * bridge programs the SDPs from.
+	 */
+	return conn_state &&
+	       (conn_state->colorspace != DRM_MODE_COLORIMETRY_DEFAULT ||
+		conn_state->hdr_output_metadata);
 }
 
 bool msm_dp_wide_bus_available(const struct msm_dp *msm_dp_display)
